TIP:  Alright, what’s the deal with all of these bleedin’ repeating chords?  I’ve put them in there as a timing device to help you keep pace with the song.  Get the strumming pattern down first, which goes D-UDU D-UDU.  The repeating chords occur every half-bar so on each D-UDU.  You’ll hear it as soon as you start playing the song.

TIP:  The second verse, where the children come in, begins a capella but I find it much easier to keep strumming the (Am)s over the top of that first line. 

TIP:  Hopefully you’ve got a mate who can play David’s outro solo.  If not, play as many (Am)s as you want and then fade out or end with a single strum.
  

